.TH AUSHA-RECV 1 "2026-09-20" "ausha @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ausha-recv \- play a stream from an Ausha sender
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ausha-recv
.BI \-\-host " ip"
.BI \-\-token " token"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ausha-recv
is the desktop receiver. It pairs with an
.BR ausha (1)
sender on the local network and plays what that machine is playing. Both the
address and the token are printed by the sender on start.
.PP
It runs the same receive pipeline as the Android app: a jitter buffer, Opus
in-band FEC, packet loss concealment and continuous clock drift correction, so
playback neither runs dry nor drifts on a network that loses and reorders
packets. Samples go to a player process
.RB ( pacat ", " aplay " or " ffplay )
chosen with
.BR \-\-sink .
.PP
Statistics print while it runs. A rising
.I underruns
count means the link cannot keep up: lower the sender's bitrate, or ask for
more buffering with
.BR "\-\-latency stable" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ip"
Sender address. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " token"
Pairing token the sender printed. Required, and it changes on every sender
restart unless the sender pins it with
.BR \-\-token .
.TP
.BI \-\-control\-port " port"
Sender control port. Default 6996.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Name shown on the sender. Defaults to this host's name.
.TP
.BI \-\-sink " program"
Where samples go:
.BR pacat ", " aplay ", " ffplay ", or " null .
Default is the first of those found.
.TP
.BI \-\-sink\-latency " ms"
Requested device latency. Default 20.
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-for " seconds"
Exit after this long, for soak testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-latency " preset"
.BR low ", " balanced ", " stable " or " voice .
Default
.BR balanced .
Deeper buffering survives a worse network but adds delay.
.TP
.B \-\-uplink\-tone
Send a 440 Hz tone up the microphone channel, to check a sender's
.B \-\-uplink
virtual microphone without a phone.
.TP
.BI \-\-simulate\-loss " pct"
Drop this percentage of received packets, to exercise concealment against a
real sender.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Play what the sender at 192.168.1.10 is playing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ausha\-recv \-\-host 192.168.1.10 \-\-token abc123
.EE
.RE
.PP
Ride out a network that loses packets, at the cost of some delay:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ausha\-recv \-\-host 192.168.1.10 \-\-token abc123 \-\-latency stable
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
One of
.BR pacat (1)
from pulseaudio-utils,
.BR aplay (1)
from alsa-utils, or
.BR ffplay (1)
from ffmpeg.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ausha (1),
.BR pacat (1),
.BR aplay (1)
.PP
Full documentation at
.UR https://github.com/aaxis-em/ausha
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/aaxis-em/ausha/issues
.UE .
